Subject: [PATCH 09501/11362] status.md close-out: acceptance run landed, and
 the baseline claim was wrong

Two things this records, and the correction matters more than the result.

CORRECTION. The section above states a "0 levels completed on all five"
baseline. That was wrong. It came from reading `levels_completed`, a key that
does not exist on these harness rows, while the correct key `levels` sat beside
it; `.get()` turned a misremembered name into a plausible zero. The baseline
solved THREE levels. The error propagated into a subagent's brief and an AVO
comparison before anyone opened the value. Appended rather than edited so a
reader sees what was believed and when it changed.

RESULT. The acceptance run completed 5/5 with shipped defaults. World models 0
-> 3, which proves the induction fix; the diagnosis was exact, all 78 baseline
generations terminating at precisely responses x 4096. Levels 3 -> 4: one game
gained one level, three unchanged, and two rows are llm_on_row_valid false (one
lost its cell to an orphaned llama-server contending on GPU 1). So the entry
states plainly that this is "restored a broken mechanism", not a solve-rate
result, and that world models were not the difference between solving nothing
and solving something.

The open list is carried forward unchanged: the undiagnosed submission ERROR,
the exhausted Kaggle quota blocking the qwen3_xml probe that tool calls on the
scored path depend on, and a supervisor that now has a ledger but has still
never produced a valid A/B.

